@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Downstream workarounds & known gaps
+
+Entries that only exist in this fork. [WORKAROUNDS.md](./WORKAROUNDS.md) tracks upstream's list and
+stays identical to ryan4yin/nix-config, so syncing from upstream never conflicts on row content.
+
+Use the same rules as upstream: the change that introduces a workaround adds a row here in the same
+commit, with a concrete **removal condition**, and rows are refreshed or set to `removed` once that
+condition is met. IDs use a separate `DS-` series so they can never collide with upstream's `WA-`
+numbers, and a row that turns out to be generally useful should be sent upstream and then deleted
+from this file.
+
+## Pins
+
+A version or revision pinned for a reason that can go away.
+
+| ID     | What & where                                                                                                         | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Removal condition                                                                                         | Added      | Revisit              | Status |
+| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- | ------ |
+| DS-002 | `opencode2dsh` pinned to fork commit `c91dcae` with `patches = [ ]` — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/dsh/default.nix` | upstream did not take the IP-pool line or the free-lane inference-surface fix (#310); the fork branch is a real merge of upstream, so syncing is an ordinary merge instead of three drifting patch files                                                                                                                                 | Drop the override once nur-DataEraserC's `opencode2dsh` carries both changes, then delete the fork branch | 2026-10-22 | on nur bump          | active |
+| DS-003 | `qq-bridge` built from the `qq-bridge-fork` input (`master-downstream`) — `flake.nix`, same module                   | upstream 0.2.0-r4 plus downstream extensions (`qq_get_message_media`); every sync means push the fork, `nix flake update qq-bridge-fork`, then bump `qqBridgeVersion` and `qqBridgeNpmDepsHash`, which also feed the bridge service, the DSH MCP servers and the agent presets, and pin `qq-mode-console`'s src/version/npmDeps to match | Drop the fork once its downstream changes are upstream and nur's package carries them                     | 2026-10-22 | on qq-bridge release | active |
+
+## Workarounds
+
+A setting that works around a bug or a hardware quirk.
+
+| ID     | What & where                                                                                                                                                               | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | Removal condition                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Added      | Revisit               | Status |
+| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------- | ------ |
+| DS-001 | distrust the eMudhra roots through `security.pki.caCertificateBlacklist` — `modules/base/security.nix`                                                                     | eight eMudhra intermediate CA private keys were recoverable from the certificates; their chains anchor at `emSign ECC Root CA - G3` and, for the Sectigo cross-signs, `Comodo AAA Services root`, and NixOS can only distrust trust anchors ([advisory](https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/)) | Drop once the pinned nixpkgs ships nss-cacert ≥ 3.131.1 (or a ca-certificates that distrusts both roots) and both `curl https://dv-g3b*-emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/` probes fail                                    | 2026-10-22 | next nixpkgs bump     | active |
+| DS-004 | reverse MiMo gate patched into `modlens` — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/dsh/modlens-mimo-gate.patch`                                                                      | modlens 3.26.5 decides by model name (#80) and keeps `mimo-v2.6-flash-free` out of the vision variant even when the route declares an image modality, so the gate now applies only when the modality is missing                                                                                  | Drop `modlensPatched` and the patch once a released modlens honours the declared modality                                                                                                                              | 2026-10-22 | on modlens release    | active |
+| DS-005 | launcher copies the qq-bridge store tree into `$QQ_BRIDGE_HOME` whenever the store path changes (stamp `.nix-store-tree`) — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/dsh/default.nix` | nur's wrapper copies only when `package.json` is missing, so an upgrade left old code in home while the DSH MCP servers ran the new tree and every send tool answered "not found"; the store path is the trigger, not the version, so a forgotten `qqBridgeVersion` bump is caught too           | Remove the outer launcher once nur's wrapper refreshes the home tree from the store tree                                                                                                                               | 2026-10-22 | on nur bump           | active |
+| DS-006 | `dsh-settings-persist` bundle plus the experimental plugins declared in the profile template — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/dsh/default.nix`                              | `dsh-sync-profiles` rewrites managed profiles' `package.json` on every launch, so Settings-UI edits and the WebUI switch reset after a restart; declaring the plugins in the template keeps the managed fingerprint self-consistent                                                              | Drop the bundle and the template block once dsh keeps profile edits across launches                                                                                                                                    | 2026-10-22 | on dsh bump           | active |
+| DS-007 | post-process the generated `auto-fix-vscode-server` watcher so it skips hidden directories — `modules/nixos/base/custom/system/vscode-server.nix`                          | upstream treats every new directory below `cli/servers` as a server install, so `.locks` led to a placeholder and a permanent `inotifywait -e DELETE_SELF` block, the real server was never patched and the client aborted with code 127; `--replace-fail` makes an upstream change fail loudly  | Delete the `let` block and `ExecStart` override once nixos-vscode-server skips hidden dirs or watches the staging directory (a `--replace-fail` failure on `nix flake update vscode-server` is the signal to re-check) | 2026-10-22 | on vscode-server bump | active |
+| DS-008 | AppArmor disabled on WSL hosts — `modules/nixos/wsl/apparmor-workaround.nix`                                                                                               | nixpkgs' apparmor `etcRule` reads `.source` of every `environment.etc` entry without checking `.enable`, and NixOS-WSL disables `environment.etc."resolv.conf"`, so evaluation fails on the missing source                                                                                       | Delete the file and its import once nixpkgs#500104 (`emptyValue` defaults) or an `etcRule` fix is in the pinned nixpkgs                                                                                                | 2026-10-22 | next nixpkgs bump     | active |
+
+## Known gaps
+
+Something disabled or unfinished, not a fix to remove.
+
+| ID     | What & where                                                                                                                                                               | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Removal condition                                                                                                                                               | Added      | Revisit                   | Status  |
+| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------- | ------- |
+| DS-009 | `pkgs.dsh.bundles.message-edit` removed from the bundle list — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/dsh/default.nix`                                                              | upstream deleted the standalone bundle (`no longer maintained`); the edit-and-resend UI now ships inside the official `dsh-web-ui` bundle as `@linxin666/dsh-client-ui-message-edit`, already enabled by `defaultWebEntry`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Done — removed 2026-11-20                                                                                                                                       | 2026-10-22 | 2026-11-20                | removed |
+| DS-010 | `dsh-plugin-guard` removed from the bundle list and `systemPackages` — same module                                                                                         | qq-bridge 0.2.0-r4 mints its session cookie offline from the persisted `client-connection` / `browser-session` signing key; the guard-log launch-token path died in 0.1.7, so the guard had no consumer left                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Done — removed 2026-11-20                                                                                                                                       | 2026-10-22 | 2026-11-20                | removed |
+| DS-011 | `dsh-agent-teams` parked, commented out — same module                                                                                                                      | the nur package targets DSH 0.1.22 while nur's deepseek-harness module still pins 0.1.21, whose peer ranges stop before 0.2.0-rc.2                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Re-enable once nur's deepseek-harness module moves to a DSH the package accepts                                                                                 | 2026-10-22 | on harness bump           | active  |
+| DS-012 | `dsh-cua-driver` bundle parked, commented out, and its `$DSH_HOME/skills/cua-driver` link removed — same module                                                            | `cua-driver` advertises itself as a screen reader at startup, so `org.a11y.Status.IsEnabled` flips to true and GNOME launches Orca for as long as dsh runs; the sandbox surface (`dsh-cua-sandbox`) is unaffected                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Re-enable both together once the driver stops forcing the advert by itself (upstream `CUA_DRIVER_RS_DISABLE_A11Y_ADVERTISE` applied where the bundle spawns it) | 2026-10-24 | on cua-driver bump        | active  |
+| DS-013 | AstrBot's python environment is filled in at start by `uv pip install -r requirements.txt`, not by a derivation — `modules/nixos/base/custom/ai/astrbot.nix`               | a dozen of the 65 direct requirements have no nixpkgs package (`aiocqhttp`, `qq-botpy`, `py-cord`, `wechatpy`, `silk-python`, `dingtalk-stream`, `xinference-client`, `shipyard-*-sdk`, `markitdown-no-magika`, `python-ripgrep`) and upstream publishes no lock file, so a `buildPythonApplication` port means one hand-written derivation per missing package plus an override per floating bound, and it breaks again when upstream adds a dependency; the first start therefore needs network access and the resolved wheel set drifts with the version ranges | Move to `buildPythonApplication` (or uv2nix over a committed `uv.lock`) once upstream locks its dependencies and the missing packages are packaged              | 2026-10-28 | on AstrBot bump           | active  |
+| DS-014 | `multi-instance` accepts `codebuddy` as an alias of canonical `codebuddy-acp`, and WebMux declares the old exact argv — `agent-accounts.nix`, `hosts/idols-ai/default.nix` | WebMux seeds `launch-configs.json` only once, so an existing CodeBuddy entry can still invoke `multi-instance codebuddy 1`; rewriting that user-managed file would violate its persistence contract                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Remove the alias and old exact WebMux binding after every retained WebMux state directory has no config whose `cmd` is `["multi-instance","codebuddy","1"]`     | 2026-11-11 | after launch-config audit | active  |
